welfare and some rap song Pops died, can't let his name go in vain I learned to fight young in the heat and the rain Buses run late, but the hunger run deep Dreams buried where the snow don't need sleep It's cold in the DNI, just talking the weather Pain in my chest, gotta hold it all together No hand to guide me, just shadows and prayers Grew up all alone in a world that don't care I'm still standing, nigga scars and all Trying to climb up a ladder even when it falls Detroit raised me, being broke made me It's cold in the deep and it better never change I came from the cold but I'm breaking the chains Turn my struggles into strength, turn my losses into gains No father to show me, I became a god Now my son got a boss standing right by his side The city tried to fold me, left me in a storm But I rose from the ashes, a legacy was born I ain't just surviving, I'm changing the name Breaking all the curses that was running through my veins I ain't on school, lunch trays, I wore hand-me-down fits Teacher said I was smart, I ain't believe in one bit Friends got locked, so I'm going to the grade Every day I gamble with your life on the pavement Learn to trust silence, keep my circle tight Nobody to call, just street lights at night A fire in my chest and a pen on my hand Writing verses like maps, trying to find who I am Come on, how can I teach you what I am?"}, {"start": "00:19:30", "end": "00:19:51", "text": "We'll be right back."}, {"start": "00:19:58", "end": "00:20:43", "text": "We'll be right back. We'll see you next time."}, {"start": "00:31:05", "end": "00:31:43", "text": "I was hoping that me and you can run it back, looky. Nostalgia makes you really miss the way I make the kiddies seem like karaoke. And I can be the tenant to your auto. And I can stroke good like an art show. Stroke good like a toss on Magda Marco. But do not get addicted like Narcos. Soft lunch. I can feel your vibes 100 miles away. 11 p.m. when it haunts your brain. 12 a.m. texting what you do.